{
 "summary": "Checkout requests are timing out at the gateway (504s, p95 up to 4.7s) because orders POST /orders is slow. Traces put nearly all of the time in orders' own work on release 2.8.3, which was deployed at 10:56:42Z, about 11-15s before the latency and timeouts began. Inventory is healthy, and orders itself reports no 5xx.",
 "root_cause": {
  "statement": "Orders release 2.8.3, deployed at 10:56:42Z, made POST /orders slow. The added time is spent inside orders itself (about 2.3-3.0s of self time), which exceeds the gateway's roughly 3s timeout and produces 504s on POST /checkout. The link is timing plus trace self time; no code-level cause is visible in this evidence.",
  "service": "orders",
  "confidence": "high",
  "evidence_ids": [
   "ev-ee738941a2ce",
   "ev-f4bc5d110561",
   "ev-9598d3c5b9ef",
   "ev-de03d0184d96",
   "ev-6e3519b0d5a0"
  ]
 },
 "contributing_factors": [
  {
   "statement": "The gateway appears to time out calls to orders at about 3s: failing traces end at 3.01-3.03s with a 504. Slow orders responses under that limit still succeed with a 201.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-f4bc5d110561",
    "ev-9598d3c5b9ef",
    "ev-6e3519b0d5a0"
   ]
  }
 ],
