   ]
  }
 ],
 "ruled_out": [
  {
   "statement": "Inventory is not the cause: p95 latency stayed around 46ms with 0% errors.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-801067e77993"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "The gateway is not the origin, although it reports the errors: dominant self time is in orders, and the gateway logs show it waiting on orders.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-f4bc5d110561",
    "ev-6e3519b0d5a0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "A traffic surge is unlikely: gateway request rate stayed around 1.9 req/s (max 2.26).",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-b3e6440f0767"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "unknowns": [
  "What changed in orders 2.8.3 and where inside POST /orders the time goes (for example a database query, lock, or sleep). No orders logs or child spans are in the evidence.",
  "Orders latency metrics from before the deploy are not shown as a baseline, though the onset timing strongly suggests a regression.",
  "Whether orders is completing writes after the gateway has already timed out. That could leave orders created for checkouts the user saw as failed."
 ],
 "recommended_actions": [
  {
   "action": "Roll back orders to 2.7.0.",
   "rationale": "The latency began within seconds of the 2.8.3 deploy, and the time is spent in orders POST /orders self time on 2.8.3.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-ee738941a2ce",
    "ev-f4bc5d110561",
    "ev-de03d0184d96"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "Inspect example traces such as 7769f09fd69ff589ea9c9222c8e842ea, along with orders logs, and diff 2.7.0 against 2.8.3 for the POST /orders path.",
   "rationale": "This is needed to identify the specific slow operation before redeploying.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-f4bc5d110561"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "Check for orders that were created even though the gateway returned a 504 to the user.",
